        "text_Hwq3AR": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Irregular periods are changes to your usual menstrual pattern. Cycles may become shorter or longer, bleeding may be lighter or heavier than usual, and you may skip periods altogether or notice spotting between them. This unpredictability can be inconvenient and sometimes worrying.</p><p>During perimenopause, ovulation becomes less regular and hormone levels rise and fall more unevenly, which commonly leads to irregular cycles. Stress, significant weight changes, intense exercise, thyroid conditions, and some medications may also affect your cycle. Very heavy bleeding, bleeding after sex, or any bleeding after menopause should always be checked by a healthcare professional.</p>",
            "text_style": "body",
            "alignment": "inherit",
            "text_color": "",
            "custom_font_size": false,
            "font_size": 16,
